A||||10||PeaceDawg||My Fiero Story||||6||
Z||000000||PeaceDawg||06-19-2001||11:49 PM||||I bought my Fiero when I was 21 and let me tell you, I had never seen anything like it.<BR>To tell you the truth I really didn't know much about the car or really even what they looked like (I wasn't big into cars)...I just knew that the engines caught on fire.<BR>The first time that I drove it I thought I had died and gone to heaven.  It was so different from my previous two cars (a dodge omni and a ford escort).  I remember looking at the red gauges and thinking wow...this is so cool. The stereo was far superior even though it was stock and let me tell you nothing ever sounded so good. It was so much faster too.  My previous 2 cars were 4 bangers. When I bought it it looked mint and only had 34,000 km on it so it had relatively few problems for the first while.  All of the external mods that are on it now were on it when I bought the car.<BR>I have owned the car for nine years now and I doubt that I will ever sell it.  Over the years it has been in the garage more times than I can count and I bet I have spent well over $15,000 in garage fees.  I have most of my receipts and I really should total them up sometime.  For the last 3 years up until this past spring it basically sat as I was fed up with always sinking money into. I started driving other vehicles.  You know it can be tough when you are young and trying to make a life for yourself.  Sometimes things just aren't practical and driving the Fiero wasn't for a bit. At no time though did I ever make plans on selling it.  It was one of those things I always felt was worth holding onto.  I even had offers from one person who offered me a huge chunk of money for it even though it had been sitting...flat tires and all.  I was happy to decline even though my parents ended up thinking I was crazy.  Heck I ate Kraft Dinner for well over a year to save for my baby..something I will never forget.<P>Over time..driving and sitting the exterior took a beating.  The fibreglass cracked and broke away...same with the paint...damage to the external mods.  In my eyes it looked quite bad even though overall most people didn't think it looked too bad...just close up it did.  Well just recently I turned 30.  I ended a relationship with a girl I had been with for 8 years and now I am focusing as much energy and money into making my car as nice as possible...visually and mechanically.  I figure if I don't do it now it might never get done.  <BR>Since springtime it has had a new alternator, new front end brake parts and brake lines, I have changed the power windows, new sunvisors (used but in better condition), new passenger door handle assembly, new rear trim, new front license plate holder, put in a nice stereo (Clarion deck, EQ, Amplifier), replaced the front stock speakers with 160 watt Kenwoods), bought 80W Kenwood speakers for behind the seats but they aren't in the car yet. I bought personalized license plates from the MTO and even got a red neon license plate frame and a neon shifter from ebay (what was I thinking lol).  About a month ago I sunk a huge wad of cash from my savings into getting my car painted and all of the fibreglass damage repaired. Well it is a whole new car now and I feel somewhat like I did when I was 21.  Today it went into Speedy Muffler and I got a whole new exhaust (muffler, catalytic converter and all pipes).  It has been loud for years.  Lately, when I would be driving down the road shifting it would backfire and all I would see was orange in my rearview. Time for a new exhaust.  Tomorrow it goes back to Speedy to get a new oil pan and 2 shocks for the front end.  All this stuff has lifetime guarantees and I think that is great. Before the week is out it will have a different front left spindle and ball joint.  I would say new but to my knowledge you can't buy them new for the fiero...at least not around here.  That should take care of the scary feelings I get when I am driving...<BR>I feel like I am bringing this car back to life and I don't know how much it will cost but I guess I will keep paying.  To me it is worth it.<BR>Future repairs/improvements include a new clutch (I have been holding off on that one cuz I am terrified of the potential cost), a high performance chip, rear anti sway bar kit, leather seats, window tint, engine shampoo, and all new wiring (my temp gauge has never worked, I have never seen my high beam indicator light, my tach doesn't go higher than 3000 rpm most of the time and my gas gauge is a little wonky. My signal lights work but they don't show on the dash).<BR>To save money I even bought a fiero for parts but it looks like it is now going to become a project car.  I don't think I have the heart to part it out when the engine starts.  Some of you people from this forum helped me make my mind up on that and I appreciate your input.<P>Now when I drive my car, after sitting for so long...well it just feels so good.  The Fiero is a car that makes people feel young.<BR>When I am cruising down the road at a good clip with the windows down and the stereo cranked I almost feel like I am in the cockpit of a rocketship.  Sure I could be driving another type of car but I sure am glad that I am not.<P>So that is my Fiero story (a little long I know but really it could have been alot longer).  What are your stories?  Ever been tempted to sell but glad you didn't?  How does driving this car make you feel? <P>Before and after pics<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1_18.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2_13.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/6_4.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/7_2.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/92_3.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-003s_10.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||6
